---
description: Render punctuation words as marks in names and labels, never as the spelled word
alwaysApply: true
---

# Punctuation words are marks

When a name, label, title, or other user-facing string is specified with the **name of a mark**, write the mark. Do not spell the word.

A grammatical dash is `—` (em dash) or `–` (en dash). It is never the word `dash`.

| Said as | Write |
|---|---|
| dash | `—` or `–` |
| hyphen | `-` |
| slash | `/` |
| dot, point | `.` or `·` |
| colon | `:` |
| comma | `,` |
| ellipsis | `…` |
| quote, quotes | `"` or `'` |
| ampersand | `&` |

```text
❌ BAD — "EVM dash gas", "EVM dash · gas"
✅ GOOD — "EVM — gas"
```

```text
❌ BAD — "read slash write"
✅ GOOD — "read/write"
```

Code identifiers may use a hyphen or camelCase (`evm-gas`, `evmGas`). They must not put the spelled punctuation word into text a person reads.
